{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octet_deficit_is_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octet_deficit_is_one","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L202-L207","doc":"The octet's eight states spread over seven lattice points; the decuplet's\nten spread over ten.  The deficit is the degeneracy, and it is one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.schur_weyl_cube_arithmetic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.schur_weyl_cube_arithmetic","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L191-L200","doc":"The Schur–Weyl channel count at `N = 3`, `n = 3`:\n`27 = 10·1 + 8·2 + 1·1`.\n\nThe `2` here is `dim S^{(2,1)}`, the Hecke-module **multiplicity** of the octet\ninside `V^{⊗3}`.  It is *not* the `Λ`/`Σ⁰` degeneracy of\n`lambda_sigma0_same_weight`, which is a count of states over one lattice point\nwithin a single octet.  The two facts are stated in the same file so that the\ndistinction is visible, not so that they can be merged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.sigma0_lambda_isospin_differ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.sigma0_lambda_isospin_differ","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L183-L187","doc":"The two states at the origin are the ones that differ, and they differ by\na full unit of doubled isospin. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.isospin_not_a_function_of_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.isospin_not_a_function_of_weight","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L165-L181","doc":"**Isospin is not a function of the weight.**  Two octet states share the\nweight `(0, 0)` while carrying `I = 1` and `I = 0`, so no map\n`Weight → ℤ` reproduces the isospin column.  This is what the octet needs and\nthe weight cannot give.\n\nStated as the failure of the defining property: assuming such an `f` existed,\n`2 = f (0,0) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octetTwoIsospin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octetTwoIsospin","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L161-L163","doc":"Octet isospin, doubled, in the same state order as `octetWeights`:\n`p n Σ⁺ Σ⁰ Λ Σ⁻ Ξ⁰ Ξ⁻` has `I = ½ ½ 1 1 0 1 ½ ½`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.decuplet_weight_function_separates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.decuplet_weight_function_separates","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L149-L157","doc":"**The decuplet carries no such obligation.**  Because its weights are\ndistinct, a weight-only function can take a different value on each state; the\nobstruction above is specific to the octet.\n\nWitnessed by exhibiting a weight-only function that separates two decuplet\nstates — `Δ⁺⁺` at `(3, 1)` from `Ω⁻` at `(0, -2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.weight_only_mass_is_degenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.weight_only_mass_is_degenerate","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L142-L147","doc":"The same statement in the form that is actually used: a mass assignment\nbuilt from the weight is constant on the degenerate fibre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.weight_function_cannot_separate_lambda_sigma0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.weight_function_cannot_separate_lambda_sigma0","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L129-L140","doc":"**No function of the weight can separate `Λ` from `Σ⁰`.**  There is no\ncleverness available, because the two states hand `f` the same argument — so\nthe statement needs no structure on the target at all, not even a ring — hence\nthe local `{S : Type*}` rather than the file's `[CommRing R]`.  Weakening the\nhypothesis is the point: no target structure can rescue the class.\n\nA mass formula depending only on `(2I₃, Y)` therefore predicts\n`m_Λ = m_Σ⁰`.  Experiment gives `1115.7` against `1192.6` MeV, so the entire\nclass is excluded. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:baryon-octet-decomposition","label":"prop:baryon-octet-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/eightfold-way/baryon-octet-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octet_degeneracy_only_at_origin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octet_degeneracy_only_at_origin","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L122-L125","doc":"Every octet weight other than the origin is carried by a single state, so\nthe degeneracy is isolated rather than pervasive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.lambda_sigma0_same_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.lambda_sigma0_same_weight","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L116-L120","doc":"The collision is exactly one, at the origin: `Λ` and `Σ⁰` carry the same\n`(2I₃, Y) = (0, 0)`.  Deduplicating leaves seven. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octet_weights_not_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octet_weights_not_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L112-L114","doc":"**The octet weight is an incomplete label.**  The eight weights are *not*\npairwise distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octet_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octet_card","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octetWeights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.octetWeights","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L103-L108","doc":"The eight octet weights `(2I₃, Y)`, in the order\n`p n Σ⁺ Σ⁰ Λ Σ⁻ Ξ⁰ Ξ⁻`.  `Σ⁰` and `Λ` are adjacent and share `(0, 0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.decuplet_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.decuplet_card","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.decuplet_weights_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.decuplet_weights_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L95-L97","doc":"**The decuplet weight is a complete label.**  All ten weights are\npairwise distinct, so `(2I₃, Y)` names a decuplet state uniquely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.decupletWeights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.decupletWeights","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L87-L93","doc":"The ten decuplet weights `(2I₃, Y)`, in the order\n`Δ⁺⁺ Δ⁺ Δ⁰ Δ⁻ Σ*⁺ Σ*⁰ Σ*⁻ Ξ*⁰ Ξ*⁻ Ω⁻`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.Weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctetWeightDegeneracy.Weight","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctetWeightDegeneracy.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0}]}